Experiment 3: Develop a program to deploy an intrusion detection system using Ultrasonic and sound sensors
Algorithm
1.	Start. 
2.	Initialize ultrasonic sensor, sound sensor, and buzzer pins. 
3.	Configure the sensor pins and buzzer. 
4.	Measure the distance using the ultrasonic sensor. 
5.	Read the sound sensor output. 
6.	If distance < 20 cm OR sound is detected, turn ON the buzzer. 
7.	Otherwise, turn OFF the buzzer. 
8.	Repeat the process continuously. 
Line-by-Line Program Explanation
const int trigPin = 9;      // Trigger pin of ultrasonic sensor
const int echoPin = 10;     // Echo pin of ultrasonic sensor
const int soundPin = 2;     // Digital output of sound sensor
const int buzzer = 8;       // Buzzer connected to pin 8

long duration;              // Stores echo travel time
int distance;               // Stores measured distance

pinMode(trigPin, OUTPUT);   // Configure trigger as output
pinMode(echoPin, INPUT);    // Configure echo as input
pinMode(soundPin, INPUT);   // Configure sound sensor as input
pinMode(buzzer, OUTPUT);    // Configure buzzer as output

Serial.begin(9600);         // Start serial communication

digitalWrite(trigPin, LOW); // Clear trigger pin
delayMicroseconds(2);       // Wait for 2 microseconds

digitalWrite(trigPin, HIGH);// Send ultrasonic pulse
delayMicroseconds(10);      // Pulse duration
digitalWrite(trigPin, LOW); // Stop pulse

duration = pulseIn(echoPin, HIGH);   // Measure echo return time

distance = duration * 0.034 / 2;     // Calculate distance in cm

int sound = digitalRead(soundPin);   // Read sound sensor output

if(distance < 20 || sound == HIGH)   // Check intrusion condition
{
    digitalWrite(buzzer, HIGH);      // Activate buzzer
}
else
{
    digitalWrite(buzzer, LOW);       // Deactivate buzzer
}

Working
•	The ultrasonic sensor continuously measures the distance to detect nearby objects. 
•	The sound sensor detects loud sounds such as claps or footsteps. 
•	If an object is detected within 20 cm or the sound sensor detects a sound, the Arduino activates the buzzer. 
•	If neither condition is true, the buzzer remains OFF. 
•	The monitoring process repeats continuously, providing a simple intrusion detection system. 
